.TH DENIAL-UI 1 "July 2026" "Denial 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
denial-ui \- prepare and attach to Denial's debug and AOT profile Flutter UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B denial-ui
.I command
.RI [ workspace ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B denial-ui
is the native development client installed by
.BR denial-ui-development .
It uses the package-pinned Flutter and Dart toolchain to prepare JIT debug or
optimized AOT profile shell bundles, discover the authenticated Dart VM
service, and attach an editor, terminal, or browser DevTools to the running
shell.
.PP
The package does not replace Denial's optimized default runtime.
Entering live development performs an in-process Flutter engine replacement;
Wayland clients and the compositor session remain alive.
.PP
Dart kernels and assets may be rebuilt without ending the session.
After installing or rebuilding a different native
.IR libflutter_engine.so ,
restart the Denial session once before enabling live development.
Denial rejects a changed JIT engine after another native JIT engine has already
been loaded by the same compositor process.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect the selected workspace, pinned toolchain, JIT engine, prepared bundle,
and live VM-service endpoint.
.TP
.BI "prepare " [workspace]
Resolve the packaged dependency set offline and atomically prepare a debug
kernel and asset bundle.
.TP
.BI "prepare-profile " [workspace]
Resolve the packaged dependency set offline and atomically prepare an
optimized AOT profile application and asset bundle.
.TP
.B uri
Print the authenticated loopback Dart VM-service URI.
.TP
.BI "attach " [workspace]
Attach the pinned Flutter tool to the live shell.
.TP
.BI "attach-profile " [workspace]
Attach the pinned Flutter tool and browser DevTools to an active AOT profile
shell using Flutter's profile attachment mode.
.TP
.BI "flutter " [arguments...]
Run the immutable package-pinned Flutter tool.
The
.B denial-flutter
command is an equivalent editor-compatible entry point.
.TP
.B version
Show the client version and coupled Flutter generation.
.SH WORKSPACE DISCOVERY
When no workspace is given,
.B denial-ui
checks
.BR DENIAL_UI_WORKSPACE ,
the current directory,
the
.I dart_shell
directory below it, and finally the workspace selected in Denial Settings.
A workspace must contain
.I pubspec.yaml
and
.IR lib/main.dart .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DENIAL_UI_WORKSPACE
Default Flutter source workspace.
.TP
.B DENIAL_UI_DEVELOPMENT_ROOT
Override the installed development package root.
.TP
.B DENIAL_FLUTTER_SDK_ROOT
Override the pinned Flutter SDK root.
.TP
.B DENIAL_UI_DEBUG_ENGINE
Override the fork-built JIT engine library.
.TP
.B DENIAL_UI_PROFILE_ENGINE
Override the fork-built AOT profile engine library.
.TP
.B DENIAL_UI_BUILD_ROOT
Override the per-user development build root.
.TP
.B DENIAL_UI_DEBUG_BUNDLE
Override the prepared JIT bundle below the build root.
.TP
.B DENIAL_UI_PROFILE_BUNDLE
Override the prepared AOT profile bundle below the build root.
.TP
.B DENIAL_UI_PUB_CACHE
Override the Denial-scoped writable Pub cache seeded from the development
package.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Locates per-user compilation output and the default writable Pub cache.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Locates Denial's private VM-service discovery file.
.SH SECURITY
Flutter source loaded through live development is trusted session code.
The VM service binds only to
.B 127.0.0.1
and retains its unpredictable authentication path.
The discovery file must be owned by the current user and have mode 0600.
The packaged editor attachment deliberately does not grant debugger pause,
breakpoint, stepping, or expression-evaluation control over the desktop
isolate.
Hot reload and the packaged browser DevTools remain available for Flutter
Inspector and performance profiling.
Browser DevTools connects directly through the broader VM-service interface;
pausing the root isolate also pauses the interactive desktop.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR denialctl (1),
.BR pacman (8)
